{"repositoryId":1251764208,"availability":"available","full":"tianyi-zhang-02/accretia","name":"accretia","description":"Personal mobile-first PWA for tracking net worth, income, savings, and a manually-entered investment portfolio. Public repo with a hostile-reader threat model.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":7,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-27T22:27:17Z","updated":"2026-10-16T01:45:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://accretia.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://accretia.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.195Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.195Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.195Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.195Z","stars":7,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["On the two names: the app calls itself Work Optional — that's what it tells you, and what people see. The repo and the site keep the original Accretia (from accretion: growth by accumulation), because a US wealth-management firm already trades as Work Optional and we're not competing for that ground.","Find out when work becomes optional — and keep track of whether you're getting there. A single-page, client-side app with three sections: Track (the home screen: a one-minute monthly check-in — money in, money out, net worth — with money out at three levels of detail — one total, ten categories, or line items inside each category (housing → mortgage payment, property tax, HOA, upkeep; insurance → health, auto, home, life…), each line tagged as an essential, lifestyle or splurge with a three-way split shown as you type; income can be split by source (salary, bonus, side hustle, dividends,…","Use it in Claude (mcp/): a local, end-to-end-encrypted MCP extension for Claude Desktop / Claude Code — say “take-home 11,000, rent 3,200, groceries 600, 401k 1,958” and it's filed into your ledger, synced with the web app as just another device; ask for a year report or whether you're on track, or say “set my food budget to 800”. See mcp/README.md for the security model."],"features":["Model your situation","Year-by-year projection from a pure, deterministic, unit-tested engine (documented inflation convention, low/mid/high return bands).","Careers with equity — multiple people and career stages, each with base salary, bonus, and annual equity / RSU comp. A browsable, searchable, bilingual role library — tech (L3–L7), medicine, law, finance — provides…","Derived savings, honest compounding — no savings-rate knob: each year you keep whatever's left of after-tax income after spending. But bills come first — you choose the share of that surplus you actually invest; the…","Tax presets — a rough state + federal effective-rate estimate (all 50 states + DC), fully editable."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"49b40f9c6bc8386ed36498b52d44d41a5fed4dba317dcc065ae3fa5bbb858077","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.333Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.333Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"On the two names: the app calls itself Work Optional — that's what it tells you, and what people see. The repo and the site keep the original Accretia (from accretion: growth by accumulation), because a US wealth-management firm already trades as Work Optional and we're not competing for that ground.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"Everything runs in the browser, and by default nothing is ever sent anywhere — no account needed.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"A deployment can optionally enable sign-in with end-to-end-encrypted sync: your data is encrypted on your device with a passphrase only you know, so the server (and whoever runs it) stores ciphertext it cannot read.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"49b40f9c6bc8386ed36498b52d44d41a5fed4dba317dcc065ae3fa5bbb858077","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.334Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-16T01:45:26Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tianyi-zhang-02/accretia/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:47.335Z","hash":"49b40f9c6bc8386ed36498b52d44d41a5fed4dba317dcc065ae3fa5bbb858077","originalBytes":12247,"storedBytes":12247,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["month","year","plan","app","what","npm","device","net","home","run","worth","projection","tax","engine","every","fire","last","mortgage","one","only","optional","return","bills","category","data","each","goal-seek","keep","money","monthly","nothing","out","real","savings","see","simulator","track","work","anywhere","assumptions","bonus","equity","icon","left","license","mcp","own","property","report","runs","salary","say","security","server","set","state","stress","three","when","against","any","browser","chart","claude","code","dev","everything","federal","findings","import","including","insurance","ledger","less","lifestyle","like","live","monte-carlo","new","plus","pwa","rate","same","save","scenarios","share","shown","shows","spending","src","tap","test","there","two","untick","whether","zero","accretia","actually","add","adds","advanced","annual","answer","asset","back","bands","because","becomes","big","bilingual","bisection","budget","build","calculator","california","calls","careers","carlo","categories","check-in","city","client-side","clone","cloud-setup.md","compare","compares","computed","costs","counts","crash","day","default","deploy","desktop","deterministic","device.","docs","editor","else.","encrypted","end-to-end-encrypted","english","environment","expenses","export","fan","file","fill","for